{% comment %}
  Builds a colour lookup for products whose option values carry no native
  swatch.

  Shopify only derives `option_value.swatch` from the built-in
  shopify.color-pattern metafield, and that definition is constrained to
  product categories that expose a Color attribute. Collar Charms is not one
  of them, so those products hold the same colour metaobjects under
  custom.color instead and their option values come back with no swatch.

  The output is a flat string because Liquid has no maps:
    yellow~#FFE500||sky blue~#A0D9EF||
  Build it once per product and pass it down; never rebuild it per variant.

  Accepts:
  - product: {Object} Product Liquid object

  Usage:
  {%- capture color_fallback_map -%}
    {%- render 'swatch-fallback-map', product: product -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}
{% endcomment %}
{%- comment -%}
  custom.colour is an older spelling some products still carry. An entry with
  no label is matched by its handle, so "sky-blue" answers to "Sky Blue".
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign color_entries = product.metafields.custom.color.value | default: product.metafields.custom.colour.value -%}
{%- for entry in color_entries -%}
  {%- capture entry_label %}{{ entry.label }}{% endcapture -%}
  {%- if entry_label == blank -%}
    {%- assign entry_label = entry.system.handle | replace: '-', ' ' -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- capture entry_color %}{{ entry.color }}{% endcapture -%}
  {%- assign entry_label = entry_label | strip | downcase -%}
  {%- assign entry_color = entry_color | strip -%}
  {%- if entry_label != blank and entry_color != blank -%}
    {{- entry_label }}~{{ entry_color }}||
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
